cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite both the paper and this repository."
title: "Adaptive Reliability-Weighted Digital Twin for Predictive Maintenance — Reproducibility Package"
abstract: >-
  Code, data and computed results reproducing the experiments in the paper
  "An Adaptive Reliability-Weighted Digital Twin for Predictive Maintenance under
  Operating-Regime Shift: A Sixteen-Year Industrial Case Study", including the model
  benchmark, modern Transformer baselines (Transformer, PatchTST), SHAP
  explainability, external validation on the public AI4I 2020 benchmark, and the
  statistical-significance, ablation and sensitivity analyses. The measured evidence
  is one machine (a production-line metal detector) over sixteen complete years;
  the ten additional series in the fleet file are synthetic proportional scalings of
  that single record and carry no independent evidential weight.
